# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but its shell
# scripts and Dockerfiles run inside Linux containers, where a CRLF in a
# shebang line breaks execution (`env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`).
# Force LF on everything that Linux/containers execute so a Windows checkout
# can be tarred/rsynced straight to a Linux host without a dos2unix pass.

# Sensible default: let Git decide text vs binary, store text as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST be LF (executed in Linux containers / CI).
*.sh        text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Common binaries — never touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary
